A||||10||hyhy4u||I Finally got me Some Respect Today!||||10||
Z||000000||hyhy4u||08-21-2001||12:06 PM||||Ive only had a problem with the image of my car with one group of people..<P>-girl friends.. no way they all think its "cute"<P>-guy friends..well at first but all i gotta do is give them one ride<P>-mechanics..they dont like working on them but i know a lot of them that really like it!<P>who then...Those little dumb punk kids at the auto store!!  Ive walked in oh..so many times to autozone..pepboys..trackauto..where ever and as the word Fiero comes out of my mouth..i either hear a little chuckle..a "your didnt burn up yet", or a "they still have those around??".  But today as i walked into my local autozone and before i even took two steps in the store one on the guys behinds the counter says.."is that a V6", and im like Yup, 2.8..hes like..cool..so i walk to the thermostate isle and pick up what i want..and while im there i hear two of the guys up front talking saying such stuff as.."thats a nice looking car"..."ya know the drop 350's in them".  I laughed to myslef a little as watching these two grown men talk like theve never seen a fiero before!..and i walk up to pay for it and the guys just like..is it fast??, to which i replied.."it can hold its own", and then he gives me my change and yells to his manager il be right back i gotta check out this car! As i pop the truck and hood he just stands in amazement..mouth wide open..just asking a few questions..It was great! Ive never gotten this kind of respect before!!  He walked inside and turned around and watched me drive away as soon as he heard the growl of my engine..It was great..sorry for the long post just had to Share!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||08-21-2001||12:09 PM||||Thats great! Gotta love when people respect ya for having one of these great cars!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!!!<P>------------------<BR>-Alex<BR>President of Fiero Montreal<BR>86 GT **Silver Stallion**||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-21-2001||12:16 PM||||I had to go to Advance Auto yesterday and get a thermostat for my 88 coupe. The guy at the counter says "May I help you?". I say "88 Fiero..." And before I can go any farther he says "I'm sorry..." And the other counter guy laughs...<P>But then he goes on to tell me about one of his buddies with an 88 GT who runs circles around his 300ZX... So in the end, I got the last laugh.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||7
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||08-21-2001||12:32 PM||||If I ever got that "I'm sorry" line outta somebody at the parts counter, I'd have the manager over there while I told him *exactly* why they'll never see a cent of my money. <P>If it was the manager that said it, I'd be on the phone to the corporate office before I even made it home.<P>Smart mouth a$$holes... like to punch them right in the mouth, but I don't imagine I'd like the company I'd keep while in jail.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||08-21-2001||12:38 PM||||I actually got some respect from a counter guy at Advance Auto.<P>Chad:  I need brake calipers for a 1988 Pontiac Fiero.<BR>Middle-aged Counter Guy:  Fiero.  Don't see too many of those around anymore.<BR>C:  Yeah, not too many people drive them anymore.  Most of them are under a cover in somebody's garage, or rusting away in a junkyard somewhere.<BR>M-aCG:  (only heard the last part)  Hey, now.  The Fiero was a pretty special automobile.<P>Too bad he didn't have my calipers.  But I still left happy.||||reg||14
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||08-21-2001||12:54 PM||||When my Dad was installing my 4spd OD tranny (440) at the local Tech.College he attended (retired NWA pilot- went to college for Automotive Technology!) A New instructor there was a former employee at GM.  From the beginning of the project, he'd stop by and tell my Dad "That'll never fit in there- not enough space, just wasn't made for it..."<P>Even when the project was nearly completed, he'd comment "You do know that's not going to work- right?" and similiar phrases.<P>Finally the project was finished and the former GM guy just stood there with his jaw on the floor... "uhhhh... I didn't know you could do that... uhhhh." Made himself look pretty stupid.  My Dad thoroughly enjoyed watching him from the Rearview mirror as he drove off, feeling the tranny shift into 4th!<P>Respect can certainly be tough to come by, especially by smart-ass GM types.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||08-21-2001||01:02 PM||||Yeah, I don't mind if the Fiero's not their cup of tea - but don't dis me about it if you don't like 'em. <P>I mean, from someone on the street, that's uncool enough, but from a counter person to a prospective customer??  Nuh uh... Homey don't play that. Homey's money goes where it's appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||08-21-2001||01:27 PM||||I don't have much respect for a lot of the parts employees. Of course a lot of them know exactlyw hat they are talking about, those are the good ones. But when I went to Advanced Auto and was wondering about brake fluid, the guy looked at me and in this hick voice (we're in NC here) says "Well I don't know about these here Feeee-aaaarrows but you'll need to take it to a specialist cause them here have different brake systems" I looked at him and said " I see a master cylinder, brake lines and calipers, don't you? It's just a brake system" He still insisted I go see a "specialist". He tried to tell me my proportioning valve was off, all I needed was to refill my fluid.  Dumba$$.<BR>On the other hand, at my normal Auto Zone back home in Ohio, they all know me when I walk in and ask how the Fiero is, etc etc.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||08-21-2001||02:08 PM||||The counter boy at the parts store looking down his nose at your fiero?<P> and what does he drive?! His moms '86 honda civic?<P> this is like the kid at the record store snickering at you when you buy an old beatles or Rush CD - like you are a moron for spending $15 on this crap<P>as if I care what someone making $4.50 an hour thinks about anything!<P> wanna blow their mind - ask em how much they make in an hour, then take out a $10 bill and rip it into about twenty pieces and throw it on the floor - as you walk out say - heres a tip for you<P>  10:1 he runs for the tape dispenser and tapes it all back together - not even realizing how bad hes just been insulted.||||reg||10
Z||000009||Spektyr||08-21-2001||04:37 PM||||I just keep a little mental list of all the people that made snide remarks about my Fiero.<P>She may be sick right now... she may not be earth shattering fast when she runs... she may have some rough-looking oxidized paint.<P>But one day...<P>One day she'll be reborn hard, putting 250+hp on the street.<P>Then I'll start going down that mental list of morons who didn't appreciate my car.<P>"Got an idea for you punk.  How 'bout you put your money where your mouth is..."<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||08-21-2001||04:49 PM||||MinnGreenGT, that is a GREAT and sad story.  Employees like that guy are probably why GM was in a technological rut for so long, producing outdated cookie-cutter cars that even the dealers couldn't tell apart.<P>"Always with you, it cannot be done.  Hear you nothing that I say?" - Yoda||||reg||9
